# Fallback for when Netlify publishes the REPOSITORY ROOT instead of _site.
#
# The correct setup is netlify.toml's `publish = "_site"`, and when that is in
# effect this file sits outside the publish directory and is ignored entirely.
# But if the publish directory is overridden in the Netlify UI, or a base
# directory makes the root netlify.toml get skipped, the root is served instead,
# and the root has no index.html, so every path would 404.
#
# The last rule serves everything out of flow/ in that case. 200 = rewrite (the
# URL stays clean), and the ! forces it even where a root file exists, so the
# repository's own files are never served. flow/ also holds the generator, its
# content and tools, which _site leaves out; the rules above the catch-all
# refuse them here too.
/build.py                /flow/404.html  404!
/server.py               /flow/404.html  404!
/edp_data.json           /flow/404.html  404!
/content/*               /flow/404.html  404!
/tools/*                 /flow/404.html  404!
/assets/cat/SOURCES.txt  /flow/404.html  404!
/*                       /flow/:splat    200!
